<apex:page showHeader="false" sidebar="false" standardStylesheets="false"
           applyHtmlTag="false" applyBodyTag="false" docType="html-5.0"
           title="Messaging | Curb Cut" cache="true" expires="300">
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
  <meta name="description" content="How the Curb Cut text message programme works: who it is for, how you opt in, exactly what you will receive, and how to stop."/>
  <title>Messaging | Curb Cut</title>
</head>
<body>
<c:CurbCutShell pageTitle="Messaging" current="messaging"
  eyebrow="The text message programme"
  heading="You text first. That's the only way in."
  lede="Nobody is added to a list here. There's no list.">

  <section aria-label="In one sentence">
    <div class="plain">
      <span class="tag">In one sentence</span>
      <p>
        Curb Cut is for anyone who has something at work that's quietly hard, and who
        has never asked for help. You text it, in your own words, and it tells you what
        you could ask for. If you want, it writes the request for you and sends it, but
        only once you've read it and said yes. It never messages anyone who hasn't
        messaged it first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="The programme">
    <p class="sec-label">The programme</p>
    <table class="facts">
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Programme name</th><td>Curb Cut</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Operated by</th><td>Parth Sevak, Welland, Ontario, Canada</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Number</th><td><span class="kw">+1 276 495 9311</span></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Who it's for</th>
            <td>Anyone at work, or trying to get work, who wants to know what
                could make it easier and how to ask, without explaining themselves.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Message type</th>
            <td>Conversational replies only. Every message you receive answers a
                message you sent. There's no marketing, no promotion, and no
                recurring or scheduled messaging of any kind.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Message frequency</th>
            <td>That's up to you. Every message you get answers one you sent. If you stop
                texting, the messages stop.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Cost</th>
            <td><b>Message and data rates may apply.</b> Curb Cut charges you
                nothing.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Policies</th>
            <td><a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a> &nbsp;
                <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sec-you-send-the-first-3">
    <p class="sec-label">Opt-in, path one of one</p>
    <h2 id="sec-you-send-the-first-3">You send the first message, from this notice</h2>
    <p>
      There's exactly one way to start: you text the number yourself. The notice below
      is the one we print and put up in break rooms and union offices. It's here word
      for word, including the consent line.
    </p>

    <div class="poster">
      <p class="poster-kicker">Is something at work harder than it needs to be?</p>
      <p class="poster-do">Text CURB CUT to</p>
      <p class="poster-num">+1 276 495 9311</p>
      <p class="poster-why">
        Find out what you could ask for, in your own words. You don't need an account,
        a work login, or a reason, and you never have to say what condition you have.
      </p>
      <p class="poster-legal">
        By texting this number you agree to receive text messages from Curb Cut
        in reply. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply.
        Reply <b>HELP</b> for help, <b>STOP</b> to stop.
        Terms: <a href="/terms">curbcut/terms</a> &middot;
        Privacy: <a href="/privacy">curbcut/privacy</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:1.4rem">
      That's the whole opt-in. There's no web form, no imported list, no bought data,
      and no box anyone can tick on your behalf. If you haven't texted the number,
      the number will never text you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sec-the-exact-messages-as">
    <p class="sec-label">What actually arrives</p>
    <h2 id="sec-the-exact-messages-as">The exact messages, as sent</h2>
    <p>
      These are copied from the running code, not paraphrased. The first one is sent
      once, right after your very first message, as a second message, so the answer
      you asked for arrives before the small print does.
    </p>

    <p class="sms-label">Sent once, on your first message</p>
    <div class="sms">Curb Cut: you texted first, so you'll get replies from this number. Message frequency varies and replies only follow your own messages. Message and data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help, STOP to stop. Terms https://orgfarm-7a04c62cb9.my.salesforce-sites.com/curbcut/terms Privacy https://orgfarm-7a04c62cb9.my.salesforce-sites.com/curbcut/privacy</div>

    <p class="sms-label">If you reply HELP or INFO</p>
    <div class="sms">Curb Cut helps you find out what could make work easier, and ask for it, without ever saying what condition you've. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to stop. Help: parth.sevak2@gmail.com Terms https://orgfarm-7a04c62cb9.my.salesforce-sites.com/curbcut/terms</div>

    <p class="sms-label">If you reply STOP, STOPALL, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END or QUIT</p>
    <div class="sms">Curb Cut: you won't get any more messages from this number. Reply START if you ever want to come back. Nothing about you is kept.</div>

    <p class="sms-label">If you later reply START, YES or UNSTOP</p>
    <div class="sms">Curb Cut: you're back. Tell me what is hard at work right now. Message and data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help, STOP to stop.</div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sec-stop-works-immediately-and">
    <p class="sec-label">Stopping</p>
    <h2 id="sec-stop-works-immediately-and">STOP works, immediately, and you aren't asked why</h2>
    <p>
      Reply <span class="kw">STOP</span> at any time. You get one confirmation and then nothing more, ever, unless
      you text again yourself. You won't be asked to confirm twice, or given a reason
      to reconsider, or asked what went wrong. There's nowhere to record a reason,
      so nobody can ask you for one later.
    </p>
    <div class="note">
      <p>
        <strong>Four other words do something different, and none of them stop
        the messages.</strong>
        <span class="kw">HUMAN</span> hands you to a real person, on this same
        channel, at any point.
        <span class="kw">OFF</span> turns off a standing preference you saved,
        and <span class="kw">WHO</span> lists everyone who has been shown it.
        Both take the six-character code you were given when you saved
        it, like <span class="kw">OFF 4KQ7MT</span>, because we hold no record of
        who you're and can't look you up.
        Inside a conversation, <span class="kw">DELETE</span> discards a drafted
        request before it's sent. The assistant is specifically instructed never
        to tell you to reply STOP for any of these, because STOP belongs to you
        and to your carrier, not to us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sec-it-is-hashed-on">
    <p class="sec-label">What we do with your number</p>
    <h2 id="sec-it-is-hashed-on">It's hashed on arrival and never stored</h2>
    <p>
      The moment a message arrives, your number is turned into a one-way salted hash,
      and it's that hash, never the number, that gets written down. It's there so your
      conversation can carry on from one message to the next. Your number is never
      sold, never shared, never used for marketing, and never handed to anyone.
      The full detail is in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sec-other-ways-in-if">
    <h2 id="sec-other-ways-in-if">Other ways in, if texting isn't the one that works for you</h2>
    <p>
      The same assistant answers on <a href="/ask">this website</a> with no
      phone involved at all, by email, and by voice on the same number for
      anyone for whom typing is the hard part. None of them require an account.
    </p>
  </section>

</c:CurbCutShell>
</body>
</html>
</apex:page>
